# Wave W17-O (Route 113): sweep pine — an ash-pale pine: a tiered conifer whose crown carries the fall on its shoulders, ash-grey dusting over grey-green needles, its highlight the palest in the tranche, on sweep turf (ground baked in). Route 113’s own tree — split from the Pass’s deep-green stairpine at a glance (ash-dulled vs wind-deep) and from Route 111’s thorn scrub by form (full tiered conifer, honest mass, wearing ash).
